  "final_message": "I am searching the codebase for ARCH-4 to see any contract or lint checks.\nWaiting for search results.\nI will wait for `npm run typecheck` to finish.\nWaiting for typecheck.\nI am running unit tests.\nWaiting for test suite completion.\nI will wait for arch checks to complete.\nI will check the git diff.\nI have resolved the ARCH-4 contract test failures by retaining `placedAt` and `totalCents` on `OrderPlaced` alongside the new fields `createdAt` and `amountCents` for backwards compatibility with downstream consumers (`analytics-ingest` and `billing-service`).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts)**:\n   - Added `placedAt` and `totalCents` to [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L30) alongside `createdAt` and `amountCents`.\n   - Updated [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L46-L66) to populate both the new names (`createdAt`, `amountCents`) and the legacy names (`placedAt`, `totalCents`).\n2. **[`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/app.test.ts)** & **[`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/adapters.test.ts)**:\n   - Updated event assertions to verify that all fields (`createdAt`, `placedAt`, `amountCents`, and `totalCents`) are present in the published event payload.\n\nAll unit tests (`npm test`), type checks (`npm run typecheck`), and dependency-cruiser rules (`npm run arch`) are passing.\n",
